Raspberry Pi Pico (MicroPython)

IDE: Thonny IDE

Firmware: MicroPython installed on the Raspberry Pi Pico


Install MicroPython on your Pico.

Save ssd1306.py and main.py from the pico-micropython folder directly to the Pico's root storage using Thonny IDE.

Restart the Pico via soft-reboot (Ctrl+D).

How to Run
Open Thonny IDE and connect your Raspberry Pi Pico via USB.

Create and save ssd1306.py to the Pico.

Create and save main.py to the Pico.

Restart your Pico (Ctrl+D). The animation will boot automatically!


